        "id": "paper-0001",
        "title": "Supply Chain Integrity at Scale: A Systematic Review",
        "abstract": "Progress in Supply Chain Integrity is limited by evaluation protocols that do not transfer between laboratories. The method replaces hand-tuned heuristics with a learned component trained under an explicit homomorphic encryption objective. The framework recovers known results on 10 benchmarks and surfaces two effects that prior protocols could not detect. Our analysis identifies which design decisions actually drive performance in Supply Chain Integrity.",
        "year": 2022,
        "doi": "10.5979/rn.00001",
